  "note": "createPublicSellerClient checks the Node floor like the other purchase factories, so an unsupported runtime gets runtime_unsupported at construction and on each admitted call. It refuses a timeoutMs that is not an integer from 1000 through 300000 and a commitOnSignature that is not a boolean, as the protocol purchases already do for their seller timeout and commit-on-signature setting. The README limits durable seller request records to protocol purchases and says the public client keeps none. The seller package's first-proposal test drives the client's HTTPS seller client at a public origin through a stand-in connector in place of the removed fetch client."
